## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of stability and permutation-based sorting, ensuring candidates can separate data from its keys and reason about time/space trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Stable sort
- Permutations
- Time/space complexity
- Merge-based sorting on indices

## Code Example

```javascript
function stableSortIndicesByValue(A){
  const idx = Array.from({length: A.length}, (_, i) => i);
  function merge(left, right){
    const res = [];
    let i = 0, j = 0;
    while (i < left.length && j < right.length){
      if (A[left[i]] <= A[right[j]]) res.push(left[i++]);
      else res.push(right[j++]);
    }
    while (i < left.length) res.push(left[i++]);
    while (j < right.length) res.push(right[j++]);
    return res;
  }
  function sort(arr){
    if (arr.length <= 1) return arr;
    const m = Math.floor(arr.length / 2);
    const L = sort(arr.slice(0, m));
    const R = sort(arr.slice(m));
    return merge(L, R);
  }
  const P = sort(idx);
  return { P, sorted: P.map(i => A[i]) };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to derive a recurrence for a simple constraint (no adjacent picks), then implement both top-down memoization and bottom-up tabulation. Requires correct base cases for N=0 and N=1 and translating to iterative state transitions. Follow-up prompts space optimization and practical coding habits.

## Key Concepts
- DP for non-adjacent max sum (House Robber)
- Top-down memoization with base cases
- Bottom-up tabulation
- Space optimization to O(1)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxNonAdjacent(nums){
  const n = nums.length;
  if (n === 0) return 0;
  const memo = Array(n).fill(-1);
  const solve = i => {
    if (i < 0) return 0;
    if (memo[i] !== -1) return memo[i];
    memo[i] = Math.max(nums[i] + solve(i-2), solve(i-1));
    return memo[i];
  };
  return solve(n-1);
}
function maxNonAdjacentTab(nums){
  const n = nums.length;
  if (n === 0) return 0;
  let prev2 = 0, prev1 = Math.max(0, nums[0]);
  for (let i = 1; i < n; i++){
    const cur = Math.max(prev1, nums[i] + prev2);
    prev2 = prev1;
    prev1 = cur;
  }
  return prev1;
}
```

